- **The compiled type checker checks `nat` and `int` static parameters** (2026-09-26, climb batch 4 rung N, `3f297441c`; `compile-ladder/rung-nat-checker/REPORT.md`). A size is a symbol or a literal compared by equality; an unknown one is an inference variable of its own, a new syntax-tree node `_InferenceVarInt` beside the two the checker had (30 regenerated node files, 26 changed and 4 new, deterministic), with a third constraint track in `Formula`; `keep-size-params` in `TypeSchemaAnalyzer`; kind-correct static arguments in `AbstractMethodChecker` and `FnNameInfo.boundsFor`; the export checker compares sizes (`ExportChecker.equalIntExprs` was the constant `false`), so a component that exports its own sized api checks (`compiler_tests/NatExportChecker`); arithmetic in a size, and inference of a `bool`, `dim` or `unit` parameter, refused by name. A size left unknown in a call's static arguments is refused at the call, "Could not infer static argument ... without context": this is the rung's reading of Pavol's rule of 09-21, and it is stricter than the types' rule, under which a dead type parameter becomes `BOTTOM` and the call compiles (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/scala_src/useful/STypesUtil.scala:1937-1940`; `compile-ladder/rung-nat-checker/probes/dead-type-single.txt`). In an overload set such an arm was dropped instead (row 400); since climb batch 6 rung R the call is refused when that arm is the most specific, unless its unknown size occurs in its own parameter type (the entry 'The compiled checker refuses a call whose most specific arm has a size the call cannot fix'). Inferred, written-out, method-on-sized-receiver and several-sizes-at-one-call programs check (`compiler_tests/NatInferredChecker`, whose `dot` solves three sizes at one call, one shared by both arguments; `NatWrittenChecker`; `NatMethodChecker`); a mismatch is refused (`XXXNatMismatchChecker`). Climb batch 5 rung Z built what it left, where a sized program failed at load (`3$RTTIc`) an